From 60694a4d73b3eefd305e96d170e2a55e45132a29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:26:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Steer sends a queued message into an ACP agent's
 running turn
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.8 (ask 29), the Steer half. Upstream offers the
queue's Steer toggle for Zed's native agent only, where it ends the
running turn at its next boundary and then sends the message. An ACP
agent that advertises steering -- Claude Agent (Plus) answers
`_session/steering`, and 0.38.0 carries the steer-settling fix (#1185) --
takes the message into the running turn at its next step without
stopping it, so for such an agent the toggle (and ctrl-alt-s) sends the
queued message at once.

- acp_thread: AgentConnection gains supports_steering and steer(session,
  prompt) -> SteerOutcome {Delivered, PromptRequired}; the default
  refuses.
- agent_servers (v1): the agent advertises steering at the top level of
  its `initialize` answer (`_meta.steering.supported`), outside the
  capabilities the connection keeps. with_steering_capability copies a
  `supported: true` (and nothing short of it) into the capability map
  under Zeo's own key `_zeo/steering`, so supports_steering is one more
  agent_advertises and no new field threads through every place a
  connection is built. steer sends `_session/steering` {sessionId,
  prompt (through prompt_to_v1, as a queued prompt would go), _meta:
  {steering: {idleBehavior: "promptRequired"}}}: with no turn running
  the agent takes nothing, never a turn the client did not start.
  parse_steer_answer reads injected and startedNewTurn as Delivered,
  promptRequired as PromptRequired.
- agent_ui: the Steer button shows for such an agent too, with its own
  tooltip ("Send this message into the running turn ..."), and the
  keybinding's native-only guard lets it through. toggle_queue_entry_steer
  asks steer_queued_entry first; it acts only for a non-native agent that
  steers while a turn runs (steers_at_once), takes the entry out of the
  queue while the agent answers so the queue never sends it twice, and
  then: Delivered -- the message joins the thread where the agent took
  it (push_user_content_block; the agent does not echo a steered
  message); PromptRequired -- the turn had ended, so the entry goes back
  to its place in the queue, steer off; an error -- the same, with the
  error shown.

Tests: v1::steering_tests (3) -- top-level steering support kept beside
the capabilities (what the agent advertised left as it was), steering
never assumed short of `supported: true`, the outcomes read;
queue_steering::tests (3) -- an ACP agent that steers takes the message
during a turn, the native agent keeps upstream's Steer, nothing steered
without a turn or without support. Seen failing: three probes at once,
each on its own function (any `supported` value accepted, startedNewTurn
read as promptRequired, the native exception dropped) failed exactly
those three tests. Xvfb proof with a stub agent that advertises steering
and holds its turn, in the hub: docs/assets/zeo-6.8-btw-and-steer-2026-11-15/
(the queued message showed Steer; ctrl-alt-s sent it as
`_session/steering` with idleBehavior promptRequired while the turn ran,
not as a prompt; it joined the thread after the turn's first reply, and
the turn answered it without stopping). Not proved live: the
PromptRequired and error paths (the stub's turn was always running).
---

